  [Approximated] Afterbeat skews a rotated object sitting under a non-uniformly scaled parent; this format has no skew to give, so the object is fitted to the nearest rotation and scale it can hold. The wider apart the parent's two scales are, the more of the skew is lost. (x15, first at prefabs[0].objs[0])&#xD;
  [Info] Custom polygons whose corners are rounded have no built-in equivalent here, so each distinct one became a shape resource. (x17, first at prefabs[0].objs[4])&#xD;
  [Dropped] Afterbeat prefabs carry a preview image; this format has no field for one and it is not imported. (x43, first at prefabs[0])&#xD;
  [Approximated] Afterbeat keeps opacity separately from the theme colour, which this format's theme reference cannot. Semi-transparent colours were resolved to literals and no longer follow a theme change. (x587, first at prefabs[2].objs[3])&#xD;
  [Approximated] Objects that never reach full opacity cannot hurt the player in the source game, so they were imported without a collider. (x115, first at prefabs[2].objs[3])&#xD;
  [Approximated] Objects only hurt the player at full opacity in the source game; a faded object was imported as a collider-less object plus one invisible collider per fully opaque stretch. (x168, first at prefabs[2].objs[27])&#xD;
  [Approximated] Afterbeat's object origin was converted into this format's pivot; the two measure the same idea from opposite sides, so check objects whose origin was not centred. (x55, first at prefabs[3].objs[0])&#xD;
  [Approximated] Some objects have children that disagree about inheriting their scale, and their own scale is animated; this format cannot express both at once, so the disagreeing children follow the majority. (x3, first at prefabs[5].objs)&#xD;
  [Dropped] Afterbeat's radial object gradient is a shape this format's four-corner colour cannot hold; those objects arrive filled flat with the colour their edge had. (x11, first at prefabs[6].objs[1])&#xD;
  [Info] Afterbeat's two arrows are the only shapes with no equivalent here, so they were added to the level's own shape resources. (prefabs[13].objs[0])&#xD;
  [Approximated] Afterbeat's Toggle randomization flips both axes of a point together; this format rolls each axis on its own, so those keyframes can also land on the two mixed corners. (prefabs[13].objs[1])&#xD;
  [Approximated] Objects inside an Afterbeat prefab can be parented to the camera; a template here has no camera, so those objects became roots of the template. (x4, first at prefabs[14].objs[3])&#xD;
  [Approximated] Afterbeat text has no bounds; imported text was given a block one character wide per character and one line tall per line, which fits any typeface rather than matching the source exactly. (x17, first at prefabs[14].objs[10])&#xD;
  [Approximated] Afterbeat randomizes a rotation as a delta from the keyframe before it, so its spread grows along a track; this format rolls every keyframe against the authored total, so those tracks vary by the right amount at each keyframe but no longer drift apart along it. (prefabs[31].objs[2])&#xD;
  [Dropped] Afterbeat can stop a child following its parent's rotation while it still follows the rest; this format inherits the whole transform, so those objects turn with their parent here. (prefabs[35].objs[2])&#xD;
  [Info] Afterbeat scales everything parented to its camera by the camera's own zoom, so a node carrying that scale was rebuilt and those objects hang off it - without it they draw at the size they were authored at rather than the size they were seen at. (objects)&#xD;
  [Approximated] A custom polygon that is both rounded and inverted has to be built here, and this format's geometry cannot express the hole; those shapes import solid. (x6, first at objects[62])&#xD;
  [Approximated] Shape 'Custom 32-gon Outline 1/32' could not be built; those objects use a Square. (x5, first at objects[142])&#xD;
  [Dropped] Afterbeat's background depth of field has no equivalent here and is not imported. (parallax_settings)&#xD;
  [Info] Prefab placements were imported as placements rather than as copies of their templates, with the id table that makes their content rebuildable. (prefab_objects)&#xD;
